{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139100-changeling-sorcerers-crusade-thematic-and-mood-crossover","id":1139100,"title":"Changeling & Sorcerers Crusade Thematic and Mood Crossover","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-09T21:59:35-07:00","id":1139100,"title":"Changeling & Sorcerers Crusade Thematic and Mood Crossover","content":"Another weird setting idea.<br /> <br /> After the War of the Seasons, the Firstborn and Inanimae, for the most part, had left, went into slumber or shut inside their Freeholds (Lost Ones Freeholds).<br /> <br /> Changelings hadn't any other options, but to stay. Yet they weren't left alone. Some Firstborn, notably several Noble Houses of Sidhe, decided to stay and became changelings themselves, despite Banality being harsh to their Kith.<br /> <br /> The Realms of Fae, colloquially referred to as the Dreaming, were separated from the Autumn Realm by Mists, now distant and plagued by Firchlis, with well-known trods turned unreliable and dangerous. And new paths are yet to be explored.<br /> <br /> World has changed. And surprisingly, it isn't without hope. While Kithain were surviving and adapting, Dreamers, Magi Traditions and Order of Reason didn't just wait for their Dreams to be rekindled and Passions to be reignited. They built a world, that doesn't need the Fae, but full of new Glaumor and unusual dreams. Dreams, Kithain hasn't learned to inspire or reap. Yet.<br /> <br /> Less like a World of Darkness (or our world history, for that matter) and more Rennaissance High Fantasy with Goblin Markets, Dragons, Knights, Swashbucklers, Flying ships, Treasure hunters, Magical cities, Wonders of engineering and craft, Exotic Realms of the East and the West.<br /> <br /> Crossover with Sorcerer's Crusade and The Order of Reason is extremely encouraged. Insert and incorporate other lines and elements from Chronicles of Darkness to your tastes. (Prometheans, Lost, Sin Eaters, etc.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 09-15-2017, 05:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T15:43:00-07:00","id":1139289,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of crossing over with sorcerer crusades, even in the age of reason the light of civilization has not reached all parts of the world as well as banality. The Menehune weren't hit until the infamous Captain came the the islands. So in some parts of the world pure ones may still struggle to exist, are the Oriental Hsien fallen yet? <br /> <br /> The works of some branches of The Order of Reason doesn't seem inheritally banal. A Nocker might love the clockwork constructs of some of their engineers. In my current game I have Dougal commoners using some of the old terms of OoR.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T19:10:27-07:00","id":1139331,"title":"","content":"IIRC, the Castles &amp; Covenants book for M:SC had at least one site (or cabal, I forget which) that had one or more Fae as part of it. <br /> <br /> Both the Artificers Handbook and the Swashbucklers Handbook have a lot of fun info in them that are perfectly suitable for period changelings as well. <br /> <br /> Also, if you've never seen the old game Castle Falkenstein, it's a lot of fun, involving faerie magic, dragons and steampunk tech in an alternate mid-19th century Europe. It's a wonderful source of ideas for this sort of thing, even thought you'd have to work the clock back a few centuries. If you can find the sourcebooks The Lost Notebooks of Leonardo da Vinci and Comme Il Faut (the book of manners), they are two of my personal favorites. There's also a Memoirs of Auberon of Faerie, about the faerie people in the game. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T23:01:58-07:00","id":1139364,"title":"","content":"Bonus points for adding Time Travel <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feng_Shui_(role-playing_game)\" target=\"_blank\">Feng Shui</a> style, allowing players to travel into alternative 19th and 21th century!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 09-11-2017, 02:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T07:35:45-07:00","id":1139431,"title":"","content":"So very much to play with from this era. The birth/rebirth of theater, so much marvelous music, and the many dreams of exploration come to mind. Assorted rebellions and dreams of freedom and conquest. Horrid plagues, religious wars and conquest of non-Western cultures. <br /> <br /> But what to use from the Sorcerers Crusade? Many Mage traditions and Crafts would be potential allies to be sure, as well as a vast host of human organizations and people groups. Some tribal cultures and rural folk would likely have much lower Banality than city folk. And not all mythic realms would be cut off yet. <br /> <br /> <b>Scourgelings- </b>These spirits are quite varied, and may not entirely be Weaver-type entities. Many appear more like powerful Wyld and/or Wyrm spirits than Weaver spirits. But of course thats from the perspective of Mages. Powerful Nightmare beings could have more than a little overlap here, with even some Fomorian like entities on the move and active as Sourgelings.<br /> <br /> <b>T\u00edr na n\u00d3g- </b>America was visited by the Sidhe and other European Fae before the Shattering. Though I assume that the routes were cut off since. An effort by remaining European fae, possibly led by House Liam may be looking to re-establish such routes. This buoyed by the Dream of Exploration could be a powerful Chronicle.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T12:03:39-07:00","id":1139504,"title":"","content":"If you use Exploration, the Path of the Wyck allowed the Traditions (in concrete, Verbena, which it's one Tradition often related to Fae trough their Celtic branches) to have contact with &quot;the new world&quot;. Using them to restablish contact with T\u00edr na n\u00d3g could be crossover fuel.<br /> <br /> Also it's said that back then Earth and the Umbra weren't so appart and you could stumble uppon mythical places, like the land of giants, just by walking far enough from humanity.<br /> <br /> One also has to think on antagonists for the changelings, because mages are already in their war, but I'm unclear about what the goals of changelings should be and what opposes those goals in a world where Banality isn't as omnipresent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T13:35:21-07:00","id":1139536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139100-changeling-sorcerers-crusade-thematic-and-mood-crossover?p=1139504#post1139504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you use Exploration, the Path of the Wyck allowed the Traditions (in concrete, Verbena, which it's one Tradition often related to Fae trough their Celtic branches) to have contact with &quot;the new world&quot;. Using them to restablish contact with T\u00edr na n\u00d3g could be crossover fuel.<br /> <br /> Also it's said that back then Earth and the Umbra weren't so appart and you could stumble uppon mythical places, like the land of giants, just by walking far enough from humanity.<br /> <br /> One also has to think on antagonists for the changelings, because mages are already in their war, but I'm unclear about what the goals of changelings should be and what opposes those goals in a world where Banality isn't as omnipresent.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are certainly more options for avoiding banalty for this era, especially for C20 fae. But I suppose the tradeoff might be that the mysts wont be as big of a smokescreen. Most people will not only believe in magic, but will be familiar with the fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 09-11-2017, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T15:14:56-07:00","id":1139561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139100-changeling-sorcerers-crusade-thematic-and-mood-crossover?p=1139504#post1139504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you use Exploration, the Path of the Wyck allowed the Traditions (in concrete, Verbena, which it's one Tradition often related to Fae trough their Celtic branches) to have contact with &quot;the new world&quot;. Using them to restablish contact with T\u00edr na n\u00d3g could be crossover fuel.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're a Mage, especially one of the Verbena, you really don't even need the Umbra, per say, to reach the Americas during the period. Mages, especially those that work with Life magic, tend to be long lived, so there are Nordic Mages who have second or even first hand knowledge of the sea routes to Greenland and Vinland. Such a voyage is made all the easier with weather magic and other tricks. (I've often wondered if &quot;paths of the Wyck&quot; is really meant to be more of a catch-all term for any method of mystically enhanced travel, including Correspondence gates, Spirit bridges, and Temporal shortcuts.)<br /> <br /> <br /> If you want to go completely nuts with an alternate North America in such a setting, you can have Norse settlements in Vinland managing to weather the onset of the Little Ice Age in the 14th century, with a kingdom/culture covering Nova Scotia, New Brunswick, Maine, and maybe further south that mixes viking-era culture with that of the nations that eventually became the Wabanaki Confederacy. Perhaps coming back into contact with Europe via Basque fishermen. Add in the Irish monasteries of St. Brendan's Island (Bermuda), the Welsh-Powhatan hybrid culture of Madoc's Kingdom in Virginia's Tidewater and the Chesapeake Bay, the Knights Templar guarding both their lost treasure and the Fountain of Youth in southern Florida, Chinese-Ohlone Buddhist monasteries of Fusang in San Francisco Bay, and a Ba'al worshiping kingdom of Phoenician descendants in Venezuela and you're good to go with fringe theory fun and adventure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T18:00:07-07:00","id":1139592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139100-changeling-sorcerers-crusade-thematic-and-mood-crossover?p=1139561#post1139561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're a Mage, especially one of the Verbena, you really don't even need the Umbra, per say, to reach the Americas during the period. Mages, especially those that work with Life magic, tend to be long lived, so there are Nordic Mages who have second or even first hand knowledge of the sea routes to Greenland and Vinland. Such a voyage is made all the easier with weather magic and other tricks. (I've often wondered if &quot;paths of the Wyck&quot; is really meant to be more of a catch-all term for any method of mystically enhanced travel, including Correspondence gates, Spirit bridges, and Temporal shortcuts.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I did mention Flying ships after all. Skyriggers was a thing, the Order of Reason had going for a while. A foundation of modern Void Engineers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139100-changeling-sorcerers-crusade-thematic-and-mood-crossover?p=1139561#post1139561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to go completely nuts with an alternate North America in such a setting, you can have Norse settlements in Vinland managing to weather the onset of the Little Ice Age in the 14th century, with a kingdom/culture covering Nova Scotia, New Brunswick, Maine, and maybe further south that mixes viking-era culture with that of the nations that eventually became the Wabanaki Confederacy. Perhaps coming back into contact with Europe via Basque fishermen. Add in the Irish monasteries of St. Brendan's Island (Bermuda), the Welsh-Powhatan hybrid culture of Madoc's Kingdom in Virginia's Tidewater and the Chesapeake Bay, the Knights Templar guarding both their lost treasure and the Fountain of Youth in southern Florida, Chinese-Ohlone Buddhist monasteries of Fusang in San Francisco Bay, and a Ba'al worshiping kingdom of Phoenician descendants in Venezuela and you're good to go with fringe theory fun and adventure.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bNorse, Fae and Native Americans already bought me. Everything else is just icing on a cake.<br /> <br /> In this scenario it wouldn't be too far-fetched to assume, that there might be Kithains left in T\u00edr na n\u00d3g.<br /> <br /> Confederecy, which encompasses both humans and fae, natives and colonists, magic and craft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 09-11-2017, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T18:56:07-07:00","id":1139601,"title":"","content":"And those Central and South American antideluvian vampires. Must not forget them!<br /> <br /> Really liking this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T22:31:26-07:00","id":1139635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139100-changeling-sorcerers-crusade-thematic-and-mood-crossover?p=1139536#post1139536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are certainly more options for avoiding banalty for this era, especially for C20 fae. But I suppose the tradeoff might be that <b>the Mists wont be as big of a smokescreen.</b> Most people will not only believe in magic, but will be familiar with the fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>How'd you suggest to rule it mechanically and narratively?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T04:50:29-07:00","id":1139680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139100-changeling-sorcerers-crusade-thematic-and-mood-crossover?p=1139635#post1139635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How'd you suggest to rule it mechanically and narratively?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good question.<br /> <br /> For starters, I would say that Mortals would have lower Banality than modern folk, as the mostly rural populace would have grown up on fairy tales and had a magical sense of reality. Even the highly educated live lives of Alchemy, Astrology, sacred geometry, and tales of ancient gods and goddesses.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, I would have village witchcraft (not True Mages) be fairly common. This would mostly be Mortals with Kenning and Gramayre but could involve minor magics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 09-12-2017, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T18:33:18-07:00","id":1139804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139100-changeling-sorcerers-crusade-thematic-and-mood-crossover?p=1139680#post1139680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore, I would have village witchcraft (not True Mages) be fairly common. This would mostly be Mortals with Kenning and Gramayre but could involve minor magics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Orson Scott Card's Tales of Alvin Maker series (which I greatly enjoyed up until the final book, which felt rushed and phoned in) is an alternate history fantasy setting of a start of the 19th century American frontier (in Ohio and Indiana) where low level &quot;folk magic&quot; is fairly common place, and people have curious &quot;knacks&quot; like being able to do some particular task almost perfectly. <br /> <br /> Also, Gregory Keyes's Age of Unreason series, involving a colonial America in which Sir Isaac Newton took up the serious study of Alchemy and Theurgy, and a young Ben Franklin following in his footsteps. <br /> <br /> There's a wide number of unusual Merits (and Flaws) in things like Ascension's Right Hand, Bygone Bestiary, Mage Revised, Guide to the Traditions, Mediums: Speakers with the Dead, and other books that could be much more common in such a setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T19:56:42-07:00","id":1139820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139100-changeling-sorcerers-crusade-thematic-and-mood-crossover?p=1139804#post1139804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sir Isaac Newton took up the serious study of Alchemy and Theurgy</div> </div> </div> </div>Our own world's Isaac Newton was just as keen on alchemy stuff. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isaac_Newton%27s_occult_studies\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isaa...occult_studies</a><br /> <br /> But as for Rennaissance, I was thinking more along the lines of 'Natural Magic' as a possible foundation of Traditions' and Order of Reason's peaceful &amp; competetive coexistence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natural_magic\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natural_magic\" target=\"_blank\"> Natural magic - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natural_magic\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natural_magic </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T22:26:08-07:00","id":1139833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139100-changeling-sorcerers-crusade-thematic-and-mood-crossover?p=1139820#post1139820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Our own world's Isaac Newton was just as keen on alchemy stuff. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isaac_Newton%27s_occult_studies\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isaa...occult_studies</a><br /> <br /> But as for Rennaissance, I was thinking more along the lines of 'Natural Magic' as a possible foundation of Traditions' and Order of Reason's peaceful &amp; competetive coexistence.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natural_magic\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natural_magic</a></div> </div> </div> </div>The Order of Reason loses if peaceful. The Order of Reason won by being violent and organized. Part of it is an explicit outgrowth as a revolutionary faction of the Order of Hermes. There are plenty of alchemists, Sacred Geometrists etc in the ORder of Reason. There aren't however alot of people who don't think faeries need to die, lesser cultures don't need enlightening etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T02:33:43-07:00","id":1139861,"title":"","content":"How about &quot;Empower humanity &amp; Not depower everyone else&quot; school of thought?<br /> <br /> One of my biggest concerns with Technocracy is that they made themselves indispensable and started only to empower themselves, working as a watchdogs to weak, frail and apathetic humanity. Which they made that way.<br /> <br /> Order of Reason has enough good intentions to turn the other way, given the right circumstances. And as you said, there are not enough of people, who think that fairies should die and other cultures need to be subsumed. Even within Order of Reason.<br /> <br /> There are legit Dreamers and do-gooders in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 09-13-2017, 08:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T05:12:23-07:00","id":1139880,"title":"","content":"For the most part, I could easily see Order of Reason folk cooperating with some factions of the Fae, especially if opposed by a mutual threat (such as Tremere Warlocks or Nephandi). The Celestial Masters and the Craftmasons seem the most likely to deal with fae. The Solificati and the Taftani are also likely contacts and allies, with some comparable interests and focus. <br /> <br /> To me, the greatest comparable elements among mages of the time are House Bjornaer (Kinfolk Hermetic mages), House Merinita (Fae-blooded Hermetic mages), Dreamspeakers (with local flavor), Seers of Chronus, Verbena and the Crafts of the Ngoma, and the Taftani.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T12:12:57-07:00","id":1139985,"title":"","content":"(Trying again after a browser crash.)<br /> <br /> I will mention the largely unsuccessful effort to establish the Hermetic House Golo in, IIRC, the late medieval period, which blended traditional Hermetic Arts and theories with the Aetheric Philosophies of the Kitab al-Alacir manuscript which later birthed the Sons of Ether. In this sort of alternate setting, I can easily see this effort being far more successful, with House Golo becoming a Renaissance era version of the SoE. <br /> <br /> Also, back when I finally started investigating Ars Magica more, I was mildly disappointed at how most of the Houses I found most interesting had ended up dumped into Ex Misc. Besides Meritina and their blend of nature and faerie magics, you've got the artists and philosophers of Jerbiton and their mastery of Ars Cupidae (arts of desire/social magic), Criamon and their weird quasi-orientalist focus on prophecy, divination and the Great Enigma, and Verditius with their fun magical objects and craftwork. <br /> <br /> One group that might fit in this setting, depending on how far back you want to go with the divergence point, is House Diedne, who were a mix of Roman Hermetic Arts and ancient Druidism. Sadly, I don't think they were ever really developed to any degree, being to Ars Magica what the Salubri were to 1st ed Vampire, only less so.<br /> <br /> And, as much as I dislike the group (for the simple reason that there is literally <i>nothing</i> they offer that the Verbena don't already give you), the Sisters of Hippolyta would probably also work in this sort of setting. Especially if you wanted to go hog wild with the alternate fantasy-esque North America and have the ancient Amazons having sailed there after the Trojan War to create a new home - say in the southern Appalachians or western Pennsylvania or Ohio maybe. <br /> <br /> And finally, there's this really crazy idea out there of the Aztecs being descended from one of the lost tribes of Israel. It's completely ridiculous, but if you want to embrace it full on, you could just turn central Mexico into a full blown replica of Ancient Israel, complete with a Temple and priest hood and Kabbalah using Native American Lions of Zion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T15:51:30-07:00","id":1140026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139100-changeling-sorcerers-crusade-thematic-and-mood-crossover?p=1139861#post1139861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about &quot;Empower humanity &amp; Not depower everyone else&quot; school of thought?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if they Purge the High Guild instead of the Craftmasons...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of my biggest concerns with Technocracy is that they made themselves indispensable and started only to empower themselves, working as a watchdogs to weak, frail and apathetic humanity. Which they made that way. </div> </div> </div><br /> The other, which is more applicable here is... the order of Reason is Humanity Fuck yeah! They have made a conscious choice to drive out the spirits, and kill the fairies. Now here's the thing, they might be right. Humanity might be better off without faries. Humanity might be better off without Spirits. And humanity sure as hell would be better off without Kindred.<br /> <br /> The Order of Reason looked at Dragons eating virgins and said &quot;NO MORE&quot; and if that price was the blood of a thousand unicorns well that is what needed to be done. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Order of Reason has enough good intentions to turn the other way, given the right circumstances. And as you said, there are not enough of people, who think that fairies should die and other cultures need to be subsumed. Even within Order of Reason.<br /> <br /> There are legit Dreamers and do-gooders in there. </div> </div> </div><br /> No, there are enough members of the Order of Reason who think all faries need to die, the spirits aren't our allies, and that cultures that aren't European(or Asian sometimes) are lesser peoples. That's what makes them the Order of Reason. Even the Traditions are Kind of Racist about cultures and heavily European biased.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T16:47:33-07:00","id":1140036,"title":"","content":"Whatever you like. <br /> <br /> Your World of Darkness - your rules!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T20:19:37-07:00","id":1140071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139100-changeling-sorcerers-crusade-thematic-and-mood-crossover?p=1140036#post1140036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whatever you like.<br /> <br /> Your World of Darkness - your rules!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but I'm trying to understand how one might get to yours.<br /> <br /> The Order of Reason is built on the back of Murder, its what forces the Council of Nine to form. IF it was just &quot;your magic isn't sciencey enough&quot; it wouldn't have gotten that far. I mean if they could negotiate why didn't the Craftmasons stay with the Order of Hermes and reform it from within? PErhaps the craftmasons get a hint of what's coming for them? So they and some of the others like House Golo basically form Protoetherites early. They become a disparate faction from the Order of Reason, when the Solfacti fall they may get courted into the council?<br /> <br /> The second point which confuses me, is I could more readily see the modern Technocracy be more fairy friendly than the Order of Reason just after the second war of seasons. It was one of the many things that drove the Order to act. Much like the Inquisition taking down much of Kindred society. So they just saw the faries blow up whole chunks of the worlds so they know how dangerous they are.<br /> <br /> Perhaps some deals are made? Your more acceptable types make deals to aid the growth of the Order of Reason and suddenly we have another factional war for the Kithain certain ones have protection from banality as they are &quot;real&quot; by all logical accounts.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T11:50:33-07:00","id":1140581,"title":"","content":"As a thought: As a point of divergence, the Craftmasons do not go to war against the Order of Hermes in the early 13th century. Later that century, when the Mercy Schism happens, it is the Voices of Mercy/Celestial Chorus who come out on top rather than the Cabal of Pure Thought. This results in a Catholic Church more interested in redemption and reconciliation with heresy than in punishment and crusades. So while you may have some sort of ties established between the Craftmasons and Artificers (building things), the Celestial Masters and the Explorers (seeking new places), and maybe the Cosions and the Solificati (improving humanity), they're not really doing this at the expense of any other faction. Meanwhile, the Gabrialites are this weird fringe group (as are the Society of Leopold), and the High Guild are totally focused on themselves and making money while not upsetting any of the existing apple carts. <br /> <br /> (This sort of thing might result in a Vampire set up where there was no Anarch Revolt and the War of Princes is still going on in the 15th or 16th century.)<br /> <br /> Incidentally, you may want to have the shift in Changeling history have a mystical effect on the planet, specifically there not being a Little Ice Age starting in the 13th century. This would largely eliminate the famine in Europe, and with a little more mystical handwaving, you can eliminate or severely downplay the effects of the Black Death as well. It also ups the probability of surviving Norse settlements in North America.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T19:07:14-07:00","id":1140694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139100-changeling-sorcerers-crusade-thematic-and-mood-crossover?p=1140581#post1140581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a thought: As a point of divergence, the Craftmasons do not go to war against the Order of Hermes in the early 13th century. Later that century, when the Mercy Schism happens, it is the Voices of Mercy/Celestial Chorus who come out on top rather than the Cabal of Pure Thought. This results in a Catholic Church more interested in redemption and reconciliation with heresy than in punishment and crusades. So while you may have some sort of ties established between the Craftmasons and Artificers (building things), the Celestial Masters and the Explorers (seeking new places), and maybe the Cosions and the Solificati (improving humanity), they're not really doing this at the expense of any other faction. Meanwhile, the Gabrialites are this weird fringe group (as are the Society of Leopold), and the High Guild are totally focused on themselves and making money while not upsetting any of the existing apple carts. <br /> <br /> (This sort of thing might result in a Vampire set up where there was no Anarch Revolt and the War of Princes is still going on in the 15th or 16th century.)<br /> <br /> Incidentally, you may want to have the shift in Changeling history have a mystical effect on the planet, specifically there not being a Little Ice Age starting in the 13th century. This would largely eliminate the famine in Europe, and with a little more mystical handwaving, you can eliminate or severely downplay the effects of the Black Death as well. It also ups the probability of surviving Norse settlements in North America.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely like the idea of decentralized Technocentric factions.<br /> <br /> But each change requires considering as much the butterflies as possible. <br /> <br /> Thank you for your contribution!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T18:32:42-07:00","id":1140944,"title":"","content":"Hmm. In North America (Avalon? Arcadia? Atlantis? Concordia? Turtlevania?) you have a Norse-Wabanaki Vineland Confederacy (full of Alfar, Trolls, dwarf-like Nockers, May-may-gway-shi, Thought-Crafters, Valdaerman, Spirit-Talkers, and werewolves lurking in the background), a Welsh-Powhatten Kingdom of Madoc in Virginia and Maryland that has a strong King Arthur and the Knights of Camelot feel (Sidhe, Nockers, Pooka, Nanehi, the Old Faith/Gardeners of the Tree, maybe more mystic oriented knights of the Messianic Voices, Hermetics of House Mariana and maybe even surviving House Diedne), a secret monastery of immortal Knights Templar hidden in the See of Grass/Everglades (Maybe there are native &quot;mummy&quot;/immortals there as well, being long time guardians of the Fountain of Youth), an Amazon-Anishinaabe Sisterhood of the Three Fires in Michigan and Wisconsin (Sisters of Hippylita, Satyrs, Dreamspeakers/Spirit-Talkers, native Nunnehi), a fairly strong Iroquois Nation/Empire in much of New York, Pennsylvania and surrounding areas, a Muskogee nation in the Southeast along the Gulf, and lets throw in a colony of semi-pagan Basque expatriates in Cuba. <br /> <br /> Let's say that in Europe, Spain never unified, so you've still got rival kingdoms of Leon, Aragon and so on. Christopher Columbus, rather than being an explorer, believes his divinely ordained destiny is to lead a crusade to save Constantinople - which still hasn't fallen, be it by luck or by virtue of not having been sacked by crusaders at the behest of Venice - from the Turks. So Spain still has a fair amount of Jews and even Muslims because there's no state run inquisition (Lions of Zion and Ahl i Batin, as well as assorted Hermetics, Craftmason-Artificers, the Jerbiton-High Guild alliance, Zolo-Aetherics, and a much more prevalent Messianic Voices/Celestial Chorus). France never had a crusade against the Cathars, which means that southern France is still largely independent from Paris and has it's own flourishing cultures of troubadours, weird mystery cults and wandering faeries. Henry Cabot, sponsored by England, is the guy who &quot;discovered&quot; the New World, reestablishing contact with Vineland and the Kingdom of Madoc. I'm not sure what else would be going on. But I think it would be kind of cool to have Poland as a political power maybe. This may, perhaps be a world where the Mongols never made it so far west, so you still have an unconquered Kievian culture in the east, full of Bogatyrs, dragons, forest spirits, and followers of old faiths. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T21:00:41-07:00","id":1140968,"title":"","content":"I'm cool with everything, but for gods above and below, explain - why Turtlevania?! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T12:16:48-07:00","id":1141486,"title":"","content":"It was something I pulled out of the air. &quot;Turtle Island&quot; was one of those almost farcical attempts to give a non-European PC name to the continent back in the 90s; &quot;-vania&quot; meaning &quot;woods&quot; (as in Pennsylvania = &quot;Penn's Woods&quot; and Transylvania = &quot;Beyond the Woods&quot;). <br /> <br /> Speaking of Transylvania, a setting of this nature demands - Demands, I say! - that Wallachia be ruled by an openly vampiric Vlad the Impaler/Dracula.<br /> <br /> A pity he comes 100 years too late, as Rudolf II, Holy Roman Emperor (b1552-d1612) would be perfect for this sort of setting, which his interest in alchemy, astronomy and art would make Prague a center of mystical scholarship. The same for Elizabeth I, the Faerie Queene. <br /> <br /> Still, in the late 1400s/early 1500s, you've got Leonardo da Vinci, the Borgia, the Medici, the Tudors, and other sources of fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T13:11:15-07:00","id":1141511,"title":"","content":"Might i suggest a timeline that pushes into a Techno-Mythic Age might have a quicker Ressurgence? Also how would you handle Banality in general? There's alot of similarly timed situations that lead to the end of the Mythic age at its low point and Rise of the Age of Reason(even if that gives a buff to magick briefly) as fewer of them seem to hit at the same time I imagine things get pulled back to a more. Perhaps the the War of the Seasons happens quicker than other situations for other groups it becomes the warning that causes them to pull back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T23:46:00-07:00","id":1142053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139100-changeling-sorcerers-crusade-thematic-and-mood-crossover?p=1141511#post1141511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might i suggest a timeline that pushes into a Techno-Mythic Age might have a quicker Ressurgence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, why not! <br /> <br /> The rest of the post, I don't quite understand, sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T16:01:59-07:00","id":1142327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139100-changeling-sorcerers-crusade-thematic-and-mood-crossover?p=1142053#post1142053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, why not!<br /> <br /> The rest of the post, I don't quite understand, sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Various situations hit at the same time leading to an End of what the Mages call the Mythic age. You have the Shattering. You have the Fourth Great Maelstrom. You have the Inquisition and the Anarch Revolt and of course you have the Order of Reason. You also have the black Death and bunch of other things. If you don't have say the Black Death you don't have the Fourth Great Maelstrom.<br /> <br /> Now since most of these things sort of happened at the same time if you make say the shattering happen first, other supernaturals might be less willing to make the Push having seen the destruction caused by that war. Thus you could justify a more pluralistic Awakened society(I still think for example there's probably a push towards &quot;We need to keep shit from getting out of control&quot; but your Council/Order might have vastly different members). Vampires who try to Rein shit in before the Anarch Revolt spirals out might still look like the courts of the Long Night. This is before taking into account the changes to normal mortal society that's being presented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T10:32:35-07:00","id":1142963,"title":"","content":"Random Thought: So, about 1000 AD, the Hermetic House of Tremere somehow manage to convince House Guernicus and House Flambeau that House Diedne had fallen to infernalism. But, suppose that Diedne managed to turn the tables and prove that House Tremere was playing everyone for fools to cover for the fact that their founder and several of his inner circle had turned themselves into vampires. As a result, House Tremere is broken, it's apprentices shuffled into other Houses or Ex Misc and most of it's leadership executed or forced into exile, becoming this fringe band of magi apart from everyone else. Meanwhile, House Diedne still exists as this mix of ancient Welsh druidism and Roman era Hermeticism, but when Prince Madoc goes off to establish his own land in North America, a large majority of the House decide to relocate there, possibly taking a number of Bjornaer and Meritina (say, the ones still more into nature magic than faerie stuff) with them. So, in this one North American kingdom, you have this large Awakened society of druids, shape-shifters and nature mages who are probably able to at least exist in relative non-hostility with native medicine societies/spirit talkers (and probably not butt heads too often with the Nordic rune wizards and seidr witches in Vineland).<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, in vampire-land, the Salubri still exist as one of the High Clans, and there never ends up being any sort of large scale conflict between the Order of Hermes and the undead at the start of the 13th century.<br /> <br /> Also, the idea that if there is no crusade again the Cathars, then it's conceivable that by the 15th or 16th century, the southern part of France may still be completely independent of Paris as it's own Kingdom of Occitania/Aquitaine. Also, perhaps an independent Kingdom of Burgundy. (Balkanizing Western Europe - and some other areas, like say Russia - open up a lot of potential for interesting, if not outright weird, nation states and cultures. )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 09-22-2017, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T10:52:30-07:00","id":1142973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139100-changeling-sorcerers-crusade-thematic-and-mood-crossover?p=1142963#post1142963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the idea that if there is no crusade again the Cathars, then it's conceivable that by the 15th or 16th century, the southern part of France may still be completely independent of Paris as it's own Kingdom of Occitania/Aquitaine. Also, perhaps an independent Kingdom of Burgundy. (Balkanizing Western Europe - and some other areas, like say Russia - open up a lot of potential for interesting, if not outright weird, nation states and cultures. )</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI always liked the idea to continue <i>Dark Ages: Vampire</i> kindred throughout the history into modern, a semi-feudal society, heavily influenced by Christian mysticism and Middle East mythology, with Roads of Enlightenment, High Clans, thinking they're high, noble and Low Clans not giving a damn about &quot;High&quot; Clans and doing their own thing and Tremere and Giovanni being weird fringe Bloodlines, etc...<br /> <br /> Ignoring Vampire and Werewolf metaplots for the purpose of this topic might work too. I don't urge you to stop, mind you. If others will find it useful it would be great!<br /> <br /> The problem I have here is that I'm not well aware of all of Mage medieval plot happening, like some of the things you or Lian is mentioning. My WoD lore wisdom has holes in it and you two just hit some of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T11:07:16-07:00","id":1142981,"title":"","content":"I don't think Dark Ages: Mage had a lot of plot, per say. Mage: The Sorcerer's Crusade's timeline, on the other hand, has a number of events that would lead to the start of the Ascension War (the Tremere getting outed as vampires, the Craftmasons decided to lay siege to one of the Hermetic chantries during the Albingensian Crusade against the Cathars, the Mercy Scism between the Celestial Chorus and the Cabal of Pure Thought, etc.) I honestly wish every game line had gotten a time line that in depth. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T18:57:24-07:00","id":1143109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139100-changeling-sorcerers-crusade-thematic-and-mood-crossover?p=1142973#post1142973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI always liked the idea to continue <i>Dark Ages: Vampire</i> kindred throughout the history into modern, a semi-feudal society, heavily influenced by Christian mysticism and Middle East mythology, with Roads of Enlightenment, High Clans, thinking they're high, noble and Low Clans not giving a damn about &quot;High&quot; Clans and doing their own thing and Tremere and Giovanni being weird fringe Bloodlines, etc...<br /> <br /> Ignoring Vampire and Werewolf metaplots for the purpose of this topic might work too. I don't urge you to stop, mind you. If others will find it useful it would be great!<br /> <br /> The problem I have here is that I'm not well aware of all of Mage medieval plot happening, like some of the things you or Lian is mentioning. My WoD lore wisdom has holes in it and you two just hit some of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage has alot of metaplot but really most of the fallout of it is the Sorcerer's crusade. the Order of Hermes formed to be the great bastion of reason and magic and major portions of it ended up abusing the shit out of that(Tremere are the most blatant example but they aren't the only ones). So a splinter group forms based on &quot;the origional ideals of the Order&quot; and we go from there. Really Vampire and Mage metaplot pretty much mirror themselves the Old Order is torn down by the Revolution but where as Vampire have a counter Revolution that rebuilds some of the old order the Rebels win in mage and the New(World!) Order comes to fruition.<br /> <br /> But a less dark world that doesn't need to follow our History could have a more synthesized view of Magic/Science/Faith. In the Real world the time of the SOrcerer's Crusade was also the High Point of Magical study, we like to think the Dark ages was the case but that really wasn't the case. Different positions in the Ascension war would and could readily change what is and is not vulgar to this day. Without the push towards secrecy by certain players in the Order of Reason, Banality would change. Fae may be more readily accepted and the glamour flows.. of course this is a double edged sword because people may still stab you with cold iron. Similarly with out the push towards Hiding the truth the Masquerade may not have gained the level of traction it does. Even without changing the Tremere timeline there is an alternative timeline suggested in Da20 for the Salubri rather than falling appart they become the &quot;Soul' Of the sabbat the clan unbound by antedeluvians and help them maintain roads vs falling into afew people on paths surrounded by Rabbel. the Sabbat becomes much more an inheritor of the Long Night Mysticism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T13:54:58-07:00","id":1143308,"title":"","content":"Hmm.<br /> <br /> Alternate Western Europe in 1500 AD<ul><li>Kingdom of Scotland under James IV, a land mixing Renaissance philosophy, learning and art with ties to ancient faerie powers who serve the great goddess Cailleach, a rising navel power in the north, full of selkies, water spirits, and clans of werewolves, as well as Awakened practitioners of the the arts of spirit-talking, fate-weaving, and seidr, and Enlightened navigators.</li> <li>Princedom of Wales, still ruled by the decedents of Llywelyn ap Gruffudd, but nominally vassals of the King of England.</li> <li>Kingdom of England, under the rule of the fae-tied Tudors and Henry VII or the evil and potentially undead or otherwise quasi-immortal Richard III</li> <li>Island of Hibernia, a land of multiple kingdoms and city states, including the still Nordic-cultured Dublin, and it's own Celtic Church (the papal bull authorizing Henry II of England to bring the land under the thumb of Rome never being issued), holding as many faerie kings and there are mortal ones.</li> <li>The Grand Duchy of Anjou, consisting of Brittany and northeastern France (Pays de la Loire)</li> <li>Kingdom of France, in reality Normandy, Paris, Tours, Orleans and the rest of the Loire Valley area.</li> <li>Kingdom of Burgundy, which includes Switzerland and bits of northern Italy and the German borderlands.</li> <li>Kingdom of Occitan, in Southern France, a land still heavily influenced by traditions of chivalry and troubadours, as well as its odd Cathar monasteries and it's alternate Papacy in Avignon</li> <li>Kingdom of Navarre, the Basque lands of northern Iberia and the edges of France</li> <li>Kingdom of Aragon</li> <li>Kingdom of Leon</li> <li>Kingdom of Castile</li> <li>Kingdom of Portugal</li> <li>Kingdom of Naples and Sicily</li> <li>Malta</li> <li>Italy's Maritime Republics, the northern city states flush with money and full of Leonardo da Vinci inspired clockwork-punk advanced technology, alchemical sciences and masters of Ars Cupidae</li> <li>Kingdom of Bohemia</li> <li>The Hanseatic League</li> <li>The Margraviate of Brandenburg</li> <li>The Duchy of Bavaria</li> <li>The Union of Kalmaris (most of Scandinavia)</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T10:30:56-07:00","id":1144116,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that this is a period when a l